  "implementation": [
    "NativeIdleResourceCache is provider-scoped and keyed by the original ASCII C-string cache key; VFS normalization and byte hashes do not define canonical identity.",
    "find does no IO; publishLoaded reconciles independent cold results with the first resident; acquire loads outside the registry mutex; admit separately checks a validated path/fingerprint.",
    "Weak entries are erased at final canonical ownership. Publication is marked only after successful map insertion, avoiding recursive-lock cleanup on allocation exceptions. Raw identity guards prevent an old destructor erasing a successor. Strict-admission mismatch unlocks before releasing a potentially final resource reference.",
    "World uses one current pool across actors. Readmission stages a fresh pool; runtime-field exchange, candidate clear, rollback and publication carry the matching pool.",
    "Uncached source provenance lives in mGraphs; only actual request-resource references populate mLoadedInfos. Graph-present legacy selection artifacts do not add an info lease. No portable graph IDs or wire format change."
  ],
